# The sets this repo declares for itself, over the compiled-in presets.
#
# Written in `U+XXXX` form for the same reason the builtin file is: the
# grammar allows the character itself, and using it here would mean this
# file needed a grant of its own to pass the check it configures.

# What our own specs document and no preset holds.
#
# A spec that DEFINES the character sets has to print the characters, so
# these are not stray -- they are the subject. Granting them beats the two
# alternatives: `any` would switch the check off for the files that most
# need it, and rewriting the rows into code point notation would make the
# evidence in them unreadable.
#
# N-ARY SUMMATION as the Greek letter, IDENTICAL TO, MUCH LESS-THAN,
# SUPERSET OF OR EQUAL TO, N-ARY UNION, LEFT RIGHT DOUBLE ARROW, SET MINUS,
# DOUBLE LOW-9 QUOTATION MARK (the Polish opening quote, from the CLDR
# research row), HEAVY CHECK MARK.
spec-symbol U+03A3 U+2261 U+226A U+2287 U+22C3 U+27FA U+2216 U+201E U+2714

# The marks, until the `marks` preset ships with T46: WHITE HEAVY CHECK
# MARK, CROSS MARK, CHECK MARK, BALLOT X, WARNING SIGN, BLACK RIGHTWARDS
# ARROW.
spec-mark U+2705 U+274C U+2713 U+2717 U+26A0 U+27A1

# The joiners the `emoji` preset withholds BY DESIGN (`src/fix:V31`), which
# `src/fix/SPEC.md` has to print to state what it compresses: ZERO WIDTH
# JOINER, VARIATION SELECTOR-16, and the five skin tone modifiers.
#
# WHEN T36 LANDS this stops working, and that is correct rather than a
# problem to prevent: the zero width joiner is a hazard (`src/lint:V34`)
# and a hazard fires at `forbid`, which no grant lowers. The rows that
# print one move to `U+XXXX` notation then.
spec-joiner U+200D U+FE0F U+1F3FB-U+1F3FF

# What a SPEC.md in this repo may hold.
spec caveman typography math legal emoji spec-symbol spec-mark spec-joiner
